@startuml
title Use Case: Resolve Flag - Sequence

actor Teacher
boundary ForumController
control ForumService
database ForumRepository
entity DiscussionThread

Teacher -> ForumController: openFlaggedInbox()
activate ForumController
ForumController -> ForumService: getFlaggedThreads()
activate ForumService
ForumService -> ForumRepository: getFlaggedThreads()
activate ForumRepository
ForumRepository -> DiscussionThread: query flagged threads
DiscussionThread --> ForumRepository: flagged thread list
ForumRepository --> ForumService: paginated threads
deactivate ForumRepository
ForumService --> ForumController: paginated threads
deactivate ForumService
ForumController --> Teacher: flagged thread list
deactivate ForumController

Teacher -> ForumController: resolveFlag(threadId)
activate ForumController
ForumController -> DiscussionThread: findOrFail(threadId)
activate DiscussionThread
DiscussionThread --> ForumController: thread
deactivate DiscussionThread
ForumController -> ForumController: authorizeTeacherAction(user, thread)
ForumController -> ForumService: unflagThread(thread)
activate ForumService
ForumService -> ForumRepository: updateThread(thread, {is_flagged: false})
activate ForumRepository
ForumRepository -> DiscussionThread: update({is_flagged: false})
DiscussionThread --> ForumRepository: updated thread
ForumRepository --> ForumService: refreshed thread
deactivate ForumRepository
ForumService --> ForumController: updated thread
deactivate ForumService
ForumController --> Teacher: JSON response with thread data and "Thread flag resolved"
deactivate ForumController

note over ForumService,ForumRepository
Clearing the flag removes the thread from flagged-content views.
end note

@enduml